Rainer,

thank you for your reply -- and the compliment: my recent ideas for
hierarchical TOC's and document structuring are half-ripe and have
not been implemented yet, but I'm glad you like them. The work on the
ESP journal, book and proceedings styles, especially the last two
classes, makes obstacles in LaTeX 2.09 visible, for which I then try
-- must try -- to find solutions.

Your reply tells me that we're thinking in similar directions! I have
only one comment: section numbering 2.2.1, 2.2.1a, 2.2.2 does not
strike me as sound, unless 2.2.1 is a subsection and 2.2.1a is the
first and only subsubsection of 2.2.1.

Frank has obviously met Goedels Ghost. I had told him he would
someday. Seriously: I have no solution. If you have an idea, type it
in and let me have a look at it. Victor Eijkhout also has some
ideas for a new \@startsection macro.


